{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1478859017,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWUxODg3MjY2ODc=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1110","origin":"github"},"title":"Confusing communication and inconsequent, and undesired behavior of `install`","message":"````\n$ datalad install -d . --reckless -s ../aligned src/aligned\nTotal: 100%|███████████████████████████████████████████████████████▉| 36.0M/36.0M [00:00\u003c00:00, 62.9MB/s]\n[INFO   ] Installing subdataset from '../aligned' at: ../aligned \n\n[INFO   ] Saving possible changes to \u003cDataset path=/home/kbenz/taste2_data/collection/testballoon\u003e - installed subdatasets: src/aligned \n1 installed item is available at\n\u003cDataset path=/home/kbenz/taste2_data/collection/testballoon/src/aligned\u003e\n````\n\nThe first info line is wrong (seems to state the source twice), and scared the shit out of my -- this was on real data ....\n\nAfter the command (which basically did everything right) I am left with this:\n\n````\n$ git diff HEAD..HEAD~1\ndiff --git a/src/aligned b/src/aligned\ndeleted file mode 160000\nindex 9bde30d..0000000\n--- a/src/aligned\n+++ /dev/null\n@@ -1 +0,0 @@\n-Subproject commit 9bde30de94b4d787f44ed8be6708320709a0032d\n$ git status\nOn branch master\nChanges to be committed:\n  (use \"git reset HEAD \u003cfile\u003e...\" to unstage)\n\n\tmodified:   .gitmodules\n````\n\nSo the subdataset is commited, the module config is not.\n\nMoreover:\n\n````\n$ git diff HEAD\ndiff --git a/.gitmodules b/.gitmodules\nindex 982a8ad..7069686 100644\n--- a/.gitmodules\n+++ b/.gitmodules\n@@ -9,4 +9,4 @@\n        url = ./src/aligned\n [submodule \"src/aligned\"]\n        path = src/aligned\n-       url = ./src/aligned\n+       url = /some/abs/path/collection/aligned\n````\n\nThere are two things to this:\n\n1. I gave a relative path to install from, but an absolute path was recorded. I don't think that is a good idea.\n2. you can see that a submodule was registered at that location before -- which I had accidentally `rm`'ed before running this command.\n\nAuto-saving had commit that change before installation, but only like so:\n\n````\n$ git diff HEAD~2..HEAD~1 -- src/\ndiff --git a/src/aligned b/src/aligned\ndeleted file mode 120000\nindex c800611..0000000\n--- a/src/aligned\n+++ /dev/null\n@@ -1 +0,0 @@\n-../../aligned/\n\\ No newline at end of file\n````\n\nI am not sure what should actually happen in this. It seems somewhat correct behavior, as in I could simply reobtain the deleted subdataset, but I wanted to bring it up nevertheless,","files":null}]}